<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Crushing force with nobody behind it: a ceiling coming down (RimWorld: Damages_MeleeWeapon.xml's Crush,
    dealt by Verse.RoofCollapserImmediate with DamageInfo.SourceCategory.Collapse and a null instigator).

    Its own file rather than an addition to Damages.xml, per CLAUDE.md's "add a file rather than edit a shared
    one" — DefLoader.AddDirectory loads every XML under DamageDefs recursively, so this needs no shared edit.

    Why this Def had to exist before anything else in this module could be believed: Building's roof collapse
    dealt Blunt, and Blunt's deathMessage is "{0} has been beaten to death." Every citizen crushed under a
    roof therefore reported as a citizen beaten to death by another citizen, which is how docs/WORK-REGISTER.md
    §9a came to record an entire settlement's first week as murder (§10 corrected the reading but not the Def).
    Fields are RimWorld's own, minus the ones this port has no reader for: workerClass defaults to
    DamageWorker_AddInjury exactly as there, impactSoundType and overkillPctToDestroyPart do not exist here,
    and harmAllLayersUntilOutside is deliberately left off. RimWorld's Crush sets it, but this port's own
    Blunt — which sets it in RimWorld too — already omits it, because no line of src/ reads the flag
    (tests/Wiring/dormant-seams.txt records that gap and why). Authoring it here would only put a value in
    content that nothing can honour, and would move a seam the audit has already reviewed into a worse
    category. It comes back with the apparel-layer damage path, alongside isExplosive.
  -->

  <DamageDef>
    <defName>Crush</defName>
    <label>crush</label>
    <hediff>Crush</hediff>
    <hediffSkin>Cut</hediffSkin>
    <hediffSolid>Crack</hediffSolid>
    <armorCategory>Blunt</armorCategory>
    <deathMessage>{0} has been crushed to death.</deathMessage>
  </DamageDef>

</Defs>
